.TH GWAY-KIOSK-STATUS 1 "2026-10-23" "GWAY local tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gway-kiosk-status \- serve the local GWAY AP, RFID, and FTP-drop kiosk page
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gway-kiosk-status
[\fB--host\fR ADDRESS]
[\fB--port\fR PORT]
[\fB--json\fR]
[\fB--self-test\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gway-kiosk-status
serves a loopback-only kiosk dashboard for this host. The page reads local AP
status, the last published RFID scan, the LCD publisher's public system-info
frames, and regular-file metadata from the existing FTP drop directory. It
never displays AP credentials or file contents, and it does not operate,
reconfigure, or proxy the LCD or FTP services.
.PP
When the Bastion verifier reports a present key, the system-status panel offers
the existing guarded
.B kiosk-mode off
action. The request must be loopback and same-origin, and the command verifies
the key again before changing kiosk mode. The status service retains
.B NoNewPrivileges=yes
and the action receives Polkit permission only to start
.B gway-hdmi-kiosk-layout.service .
.PP
The installed system service listens on
.BR http://127.0.0.1:8899/ .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --host ADDRESS
Bind address. The default is 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.B --port PORT
Bind port. The default is 8899.
.TP
.B --json
Print one kiosk JSON payload and exit.
.TP
.B --self-test
Build one page, validate key sections, and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GWAY_FTP_DROP_DIRECTORY
FTP drop directory to list. Defaults to /srv/prodigy-ftp/drop.
.TP
.B GWAY_KIOSK_SYSTEM_STATUS_FILE
Published LCD system-info frame file to read. Defaults to
/home/arthe/.local/state/lcd-lockfiles/lcd-system-info.json.
.TP
.B GWAY_KIOSK_ALLOW_AP_ROTATION
Permit the separately authorized AP password rotation control when set to a
true value. It is disabled by default.
.TP
.B GWAY_KIOSK_HOST
Loopback bind address. Defaults to 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.B GWAY_KIOSK_PORT
Listen port. Defaults to 8899.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /srv/prodigy-ftp/drop
Read-only source of file names, sizes, and modification times for the kiosk
FTP-drop panel.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1)
